<!--
  Synthetic C-CDA Medications section. No patient data.

  The narrative table is ordered Medication, Sig, Dispense Quantity, Last
  Filled, Start Date, End Date, Status, so reading it by position (name, dose,
  frequency, status) stores the sig as the dose and the last-fill date as the
  status. The entries carry every field explicitly:

    med-display      RxNorm code with a displayName; a dose of "1" counted in
                     the administration unit; route; start and end; every 12 h;
                     completed; an indication; a sig that references its cell
    med-original     code whose originalText references the narrative cell; a
                     dose in mg; an event-related time (at bedtime); active
    med-translation  code with nullFlavor whose RxNorm translation names it;
                     aborted
    med-name         no code at all: the product's <name>; suspended
    med-code-only    nothing but the RxNorm code names it
    med-negated      negationInd with "drug or medicament": no known medications
    med-not-taking   negationInd with a named product
    med-unnamed      nothing names it, and its sig references its own row

  Every activity is an intent (moodCode INT), as medication lists usually are.
  Every activity but med-code-only and the negated ones references its row.
-->
